SUSPECTED BUG: fmt.Errorf with a %w operand that may be nil has no entry for the wrap-of-nil error.
err := fmt.Errorf("void %d: %w", n, gateway.Void(n)) wraps unconditionally, then errors.Is(err, ErrDeclined) -> nil.
Run-time truth: ErrInternal under "void %d: %w", plus a non-nil error wrapping nothing whenever Void succeeds
(the app prints "void 3: %!w(<nil>)"); a wrapped ErrDeclined is always handled.
Expected: ErrInternal with the chain and an opaque fmt.Errorf "void %d: %w" entry for the wrap of nil.
Actual: ErrInternal, and ErrDeclined kept as possibly handled "wrapped value may be nil" (the documented
conservative rule, e2e guards/is_errorf_nil_operand) - but nothing that stands for the nil-wrapping error.
